# Queue system

- **Workers live in `apps/worker`** (separate Node process) — never inside Next.js handlers
- Queues defined in `packages/lib/queue`: `extract_receipt`, `generate_insights`
- Retry with exponential backoff (max 5 attempts); failed jobs surface in `Receipt.status = failed` or `needs_review`
- Idempotent handlers:
  - `extract_receipt`: keyed on `receiptId`; safe to replay
  - `generate_insights`: debounced per user; Insight upsert keyed on `(userId, contentFingerprint)`
- Always call AI service via the worker (never the web tier) and send `X-Internal-Token`
- Persist every AI call as an `ExtractionAttempt` row (raw JSON + usage + cost)
- Set `Receipt.status = needs_review` when any critical field confidence < 0.7

## Testing

Mock AI HTTP client, Prisma, S3, and Redis. Required cases:

| Scenario | Expected |
|----------|----------|
| Happy path | Receipt populated, ExtractionAttempt row, generate_insights enqueued |
| AI timeout | Retry scheduled, no partial state |
| Duplicate job id | Idempotent — no duplicate rows |
| Low confidence | `Receipt.status = needs_review`, fields still saved |
| Malformed AI response | Fail fast, no retry storm, ExtractionAttempt logged with status=failed |

## Dev tooling

- Bull Board mounted at `/admin/queues` in dev only, behind auth
